# Help guideline + in-product `?` link

When you add or change a **user-visible** capability (designer tab, dialog, Admin
menu, Portal page — anything a person ticks, types, or saves), ship **both**:

1. A Guidelines article on `frontend/help` (catalog + `NAV_TREE` menu path).
2. A red **`?`** on that screen (same pattern as Table Design → Formula) that
   opens the article in a new tab.

Do not ship the UI without the `?`. Do not invent a second docs site.

## How to write the article

Follow skill **`extract-help-guideline`**: output the 提取清单, **wait for 确认**,
then write `frontend/help`. Hang the leaf under the **same menu** as the product
(DW sidebar / Function Unit tab / Admin / Portal). Capture figures with
`frontend/scripts/capture-help-guide-images.mjs` and **redact** emails, names,
and process ids before they land in `public/guides/`.

## How to add the `?`

Copy `frontend/developer-workstation/src/components/designer/DesignerHelpLink.vue`
(or the same markup: `QuestionFilled`, `target="_blank"`, `rel="noopener noreferrer"`).

```vue
<DesignerHelpLink
  path="/email-send#connection"
  :aria-label="t('connection.guideLinkAria')"
  test-id="connection-guide-link"
/>
```

URL helper: `helpGuideAbsoluteUrl()` in
`frontend/developer-workstation/src/utils/computedFieldGuide.ts`
→ `${origin}/help/<id>` (not `/dev/help/…`).

Place the icon **next to the feature title** (dialog header, toolbar beside the
primary action, or properties section heading) — not buried in a tooltip-only
control.

i18n: `guideLinkAria` in en / zh-CN / zh-TW in the same change.

## When this does not apply

Pure backend/API, schema-only, tests, deploy, or agent rules/skills with no
designer/admin/portal surface.
